      "start": 1500,
      "details": "<p class=\"p1\"><em>Cebel-i Dem\u0101vend</em>:\u00a0It lies on the frontier of <em>Rey</em> (modern Ray<em data-start=\"196\" data-end=\"207\">, Iran</em>). At times it can be seen from <em>S\u0101ve</em> (modern Saveh, Iran). The dome-shaped summit in the middle becomes visible. And at all times there is no lack of smoke rising from its top. Truly, no one has ever climbed to its very peak. According to some, the Prophet <em>S\u00fcleym\u0101n</em>\u2014peace be upon him\u2014confined the <em>\u1e63a\u1e2bre</em> jinn there. Likewise <em>Efr\u012bd\u016bn</em> imprisoned <em>\u1e0ca\u1e25\u1e25\u0101k</em> there as well.\u00a0It is related from <em>Mis\u2018ar bin M\u00fchelhil</em> that he climbed up to half of it with a thousand hardships\u2014though many times he nearly fell and perished. And he reached a fissure from which <em data-start=\"781\" data-end=\"797\">kibr\u012bt-i a\u1e25mer</em> (red sulphur) flowed. All around it the substance solidified and froze. But when the sun rose, it would ignite and become a blazing fire.\u00a0It is transmitted from the inhabitants of the villages on the mountain\u2019s slopes that whenever ants swarm around <em>K\u016bh-i Dem\u0101vend</em> (modern <em data-start=\"1078\" data-end=\"1100\">Mount </em>Damavand<em data-start=\"1078\" data-end=\"1100\">, Iran</em>), famine and scarcity unfailingly appear in those regions. Whenever snow and rain fall continuously on the mountain\u2019s skirts, the people of the surrounding lands pour goat\u2019s milk upon the fire, and at that very moment they see the rain cease. And whenever one side of the snowcap on the mountain\u2019s summit freezes, strife breaks out in the region on that side and blood is shed... [partial translation]</p>",
